# Line endings.
#
# Without this file, line endings are decided by whatever wrote them. This
# repository has been bitten by that twice in one day, both times on
# REPOSITORY_AUDIT.md, both times because a tool wrote the file back with
# platform-native newlines:
#
#   #60  added LIFECYCLE_LADDER.md as the only CRLF file in an all-LF tree
#   #63  a 21-line audit edit arrived as a 740-line diff
#
# Neither changed a character of content. Both buried the real change in
# hundreds of lines of noise, which is worse than cosmetic here: this
# repository reviews by reading diffs, and a diff nobody can read is a review
# nobody performed.
#
# There is a sharper reason than readability. #24 and #25 established that
# digest-bearing fixtures must be written as exact bytes, because a digest over
# a file whose newlines depend on the checkout is not an identity. Every digest
# in this repository -- Scroll seals, the Magic ledger chain, record_digest,
# and now plan_digest -- rests on bytes being what they were when they were
# sealed. Unmanaged line endings put a platform variable underneath all of it.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than bare `text=auto`: auto normalizes what is stored but
# still checks out CRLF on Windows if core.autocrlf says so, which leaves the
# working tree -- the thing that gets hashed and tested -- platform dependent.
# The whole tree is already LF, so this pins what is true rather than changing
# anything.
#
# The tree is entirely text at the time of writing: .gitignore, .js, .json,
# .md, .py, .yml. Add an explicit `binary` rule beside this note before
# committing the first file that is not.

* text=auto eol=lf
